course: dictionary
lesson: 12754
title: Durable: strong and lasting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Durable is a word you will meet in science, design and shopping. It means strong and lasting a long time without breaking or wearing out. «The playground needs durable materials, such as metal or tough plastic.» Metal and tough plastic do not break easily, so they are durable.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «The tent is durable: it survived three summers of camping.» Surviving three summers tells you the tent lasted a long time. Always check your meaning: swap in strong and lasting, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Durable is an adjective, so it describes a thing. Its forms are durable, more durable and most durable. «Hard-wearing and durable» is a common pair of words, because both mean the thing keeps its strength over time.
fact: Durable means strong and lasting a long time without breaking or wearing out.
fact: «Durable» is an adjective: durable, more durable, most durable.
fact: «Durable materials» are materials such as metal or tough plastic that do not break easily.
fact: In money talk, durables or durable goods are things people buy that last many years, such as fridges and cars.
fact: «A durable peace» is a formal phrase meaning a peace that lasts for a long time.
exercise: «The playground needs durable materials.» What does durable mean? | Cheap and quick to make | *Strong and lasting a long time | Bright and colourful | Soft and warm
exercise: Which of these things is most likely to be durable? | *A steel bicycle frame | A wet tissue | A balloon | A paper cup
exercise: «The tent is durable: it survived three summers of camping.» What does the sentence tell you? | The tent is brand new | The tent was lost on the first trip | *The tent has lasted a long time | The tent is too small for a family
test: In money talk, «durables» means: | Jobs that children can do at home | Food that goes off quickly | *Things people buy that last many years, such as fridges and cars | Coins people save in a jar
test: Which word is closest in meaning to durable? | Shiny | Temporary | *Lasting | Fragile
exam: Which sentence uses durable correctly? | The durable rain fell all day and stopped | The glass vase is durable, it breaks at the slightest touch | *The school desks are durable, they have lasted ten years | The durable cake was eaten quickly
